ion or search and destroy  next up we've got prisoner rescue  prisoner rescue has hostages and it is  up to you to get them out alive or to  defend them at all costs from extraction  there are no respawns one shot one  opportunity mom spaghetti eminem lose  yourself type moment here y'all the mode  is round based and there are only two  prisoners if you pick up the prisoner  you are somewhat vulnerable because you  can only fight with either a pistol or  your fist however to help with balance  the escort team will have advantages  like a radar sweep for enemy callouts as  well as removing the mark indicator off  the prisoner meaning that the defending  team won't be able to see where the  prisoners are located mid extraction so  let's turn over to maps during the cod  next showcase there was a clear split  and design philosophy between  competitive small maps and larger ones  from larger maps with several points of  interest to smaller tighter and faster  engagements you will see in 6v6 based  maps now we got to see two of them there  was a 6v6 map in mercado los alamos a  little street market in a historic  section of mexico the rumor is there's a  crap ton of drugs being smuggled and  authorities want to seize them and  according to the dev there's a slight  warning be wary of this map during the  beta y'all cause it plays fast  serif bay is a battle map located in the  southern coast and has all the aesthetic  of a small fishing town perfect for that  water-based gameplay i mentioned earlier  the map shifts dramatically from the  waters as you move into town where  suddenly engagements become cluttered in  an urban area with plenty of rooftops  and ledges to hang from as well allowing  for some cool parkour as you traverse to  your next kill  battle maps now encompass a wide variety  of modes with ground war just being one  of them  warzone 2.0 is going back to its roots  but with an all-new map in alamarza  vehicles have a new physics model which  means different handling depending on  what vehicles you use there's also a  cool implementation of destruction one  thing i want to try out is popping some  tires to mess with an enemy driver  before snagging a kill or two there's a  completely new circle mechanic in  warzone 2.0 as well instead of having  one giant circle across the map that  slowly shrinks over the course of the  match there are gonna be multiple  circles that would isolate themselves  from each other before eventually  traveling to a final point where the  circles merge kind of makes me think of  a tournament bracket you know you clear  out the opponents within your circle  first before meeting up with the last  players standing from their own circles  for a final showdown  there are also strongholds which are  complete with ai enemies into war zone  2.0 which i'm not sure how fans will  feel about the ai i mean fortnite does  it pretty well all things considered so  there may be something here the main  incentive to fight in a stronghold  though is for that good sweet loot the  ai fortified strongholds will have some  excellent gear so if you manage to  survive and not make too much noise and  avoid other players it may have been  worth the risk  arriving alongside warzone 2.0 we have  dmz which is an extraction mode located  on the same warzone 2.0 map al-mazra the  rumors were this was going to be cod's  escape from tarkov mode but the priority  on player choice on what you want to do  go loud go quiet or just avoid as many  players as possible and explore the map  there wasn't a lot revealed and more  will be shared at a later time now  there's a new gunsmith as well which cod  recently dropped the trailer for it  allows players to swap between weapons  while offering a bunch of customization  and an overhaul to how weapons are  classified weapons platforms are meant  to streamline progression and create  attachment pools according to the cod  blog operators will receive every base  weapons platform from 